# Security baseline

## Always

- Parameterized SQL / prepared statements only — never string-concat SQL.
- Hash passwords with Argon2id (or bcrypt ≥ 12). Never store plaintext.
- JWT secrets from env; rotate-capable; never log tokens/passwords.
- Role + object-level authz on every protected route (`shop_id` filter). Prevent IDOR.
- Validate all inputs at API boundary (Zod). Reject unknown fields (no mass assignment).
- Rate-limit `/auth/login` and `/auth/google`. Helmet. CORS allowlist. Request body size limits.
- No public registration. Google sign-in must verify ID token server-side and map to an existing user by email — never auto-provision.
- Export (PDF/Excel) endpoints require authz per RBAC.
- Flutter: tokens in `flutter_secure_storage` only.
- Prod assumes HTTPS. No secrets in git (see `.gitignore`).

## Never

```text
❌ WHERE id = ${req.params.id}          // SQL injection
❌ res.json({ token, passwordHash })    // secret leakage
❌ if (req.body.role === 'super_admin') // trust client role
❌ SharedPreferences for JWT
❌ UPDATE/DELETE stock_transactions
```

```text
✅ parameterized queries + shop_id check from auth context
✅ role from DB/JWT verified server-side; re-check for sensitive ops
```

## Dependency hygiene

Add packages only when needed. Prefer well-known maintained libs already chosen in ADRs. No random obscure crypto/HTTP libs.
